    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39432" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιθεσπ-ίζω</span></b> , of Triton, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>prophesy</i> or <i>divine upon</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ τρίποδι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					4.179
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>. of an
			oracle, <i>give sanction</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					2.6
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. βασιλείαν</span>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					3.35
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>. <i>apply a
				prophecy</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ Τειρεσίου ἑαυτῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VA</u>
					7.4
				</span></i>
			.</div>
